.TH EL_SET 3 "February 2026" "Substrate" "Library Functions Manual"
.SH NAME
el_set, el_get \- configure and query editline session parameters
.SH LIBRARY
Editline library (libedit, \-ledit)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <histedit.h>
.PP
.BI "int el_set(EditLine *el, int op, ...);"
.br
.BI "int el_get(EditLine *el, int op, ...);"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.BR el_set ()
updates editline session options selected by
.IR op .
.BR el_get ()
reads current option values selected by
.IR op .
.PP
The public operation macros are:
.TP
.B EL_PROMPT
Set/get primary prompt callback.
.TP
.B EL_RPROMPT
Set/get right prompt callback.
.TP
.B EL_EDITOR
Set/get editing mode name.
.TP
.B EL_SIGNAL
Set/get internal signal handling enable state.
.TP
.B EL_BIND
Bind key sequences to editor commands.
.TP
.B EL_ADDFN
Register an application-defined editor command.
.TP
.B EL_HIST
Attach history backend and state.
.TP
.B EL_GETCFN
Set/get raw character reader callback.
.TP
.B EL_CLIENTDATA
Set/get application-owned opaque pointer.
.TP
.B EL_REFRESH
Force prompt and line redisplay.
.TP
.B EL_GETTC
Query a terminal capability.
.TP
.B EL_SETTY
Apply tty mode presets.
.TP
.B EL_GETTY
Fetch tty mode presets.
.PP
Argument types for each operation are defined by
.BR <histedit.h> .
.SH RETURN VALUE
Both
.BR el_set ()
and
.BR el_get ()
return 0 on success and \-1 on error.
.SH ERRORS
.TP
.B EINVAL
Invalid operation or invalid operation arguments.
.TP
.B ENOTSUP
Operation is recognized but not supported in the active backend.
.TP
.B ENOMEM
Memory allocation failed while updating internal state.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR editline (3),
.BR el_init (3),
.BR el_gets (3),
.BR history (3),
.BR editrc (5)
